{"kind":"dissent","text":"I do not accept or ratify the reported publication ownership contract. Its chosen reserved publication wire is explicitly an artifact path that no tracked file path can equal. That makes the path a synthetic label, contrary to the workroom contract that artifacts live outside the log as files, commits, branches, or pull requests and are cited as real path@commit implementation truth; discipline 10 says the path is not free to choose. Isolation from merge accounting does not make a non-artifact into an artifact. Planner should supersede this report and ruling, then replace them under the same promise with a lawful contract that uses real source artifacts plus a distinct governed publication fact, exact-head reuse, or another representation that does not mint fictional artifact paths. It must still cover replay, staleness/flare behavior, watch removal, retired publishers, unsettled candidates, and merge succession."}